{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now, your two sons</b> etc. What Yaakov promised Yosef — that he would merit two tribes, what he did not do for any other tribe — the reason is as our Sages taught in the chapter Yesh Nochalin, because he sustained him during the famine. And one may further say: because he was the firstborn of Rachel's womb, for she was the first and foremost of his intention, unlike Dan and Gad. Another interpretation: for the honor of Rachel he intended, that she have one tribe more than each of the concubines."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:59.195157849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}